        "why": "The L.S. shows the filaments joined to the corolla tube, which is the only way to draw \"epipetalous\"; the T.S. shows the two chambers, the swollen placenta and the tilted partition.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing the stamens free from the corolla. In Solanaceae they are attached to it.",
          "Drawing the partition upright. It must be tilted to show the oblique carpels."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Draw the circle, then the partition as a slanting line, not an upright one.",
        "margin_note": "The T.S. of the ovary with the slanting partition carries this mark on its own."
