        "id": "s4_oblique",
        "kind": "boxed_final",
        "label": "The oblique ovary",
        "marks": 1,
        "lines": [
          {
            "text": "Carpels lie obliquely at 45°",
            "style": "boxed"
          },
          "They are set at 45° to the median plane. This",
          "oblique ovary is a family character of Solanaceae",
          "and separates it from other families with a",
          "bilocular superior ovary.",
          "Example: Solanum nigrum."
        ],
        "why": "Many families have a bilocular superior ovary, so the 45 degree tilt is the character that names this one.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Leaving out the angle. \"Obliquely at 45 degrees\" is the marked phrase.",
          "Saying the whole flower is tilted. Only the carpels are set obliquely."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Everything in Solanaceae is straight except the carpels, which sit at 45 degrees.",
        "margin_note": "One boxed line. Write \"obliquely at 45 degrees\" in those words.",
        "mark_note": "Oblique ovary"
